messages:
jamal: Hey @kate — quick question. Support wants FullStory access to troubleshoot a couple of beta customer sessions. Can we do a limited prod pilot or is this a hard no? Main concerns: PII exposure, retention, and who can view sessions. Link to vendor docs: https://help.fullstory.com/.

maria: tagging in support context — we'll only give viewing rights to the support group (support@redwood.com). We need a security checklist before we do anything. :slightly_smiling_face:

jamal: Proposed controls from our side:
- read-only viewer role for support
- limit to specific org/roles via SSO (SAML)
- session capture with client-side masking
- retention 30 days for session data
Example mask config we were thinking to push client-side:
```javascript
// run before FullStory.init
window.redactPersonal = () => {
  document.querySelectorAll('input[type="password"], input[name*="ssn"], .credit-card').forEach(el => el.setAttribute('data-fs-redact', 'true'));
  // mask emails in DOM
  document.querySelectorAll('.user-email').forEach(el => el.textContent = el.textContent.replace(/[^@\s]+@/,'[redacted]@'));
}
redactPersonal();
```

kate: A few quick security checks:
- Are we capturing server-side logs into FullStory? (we should not)
- Confirm SSO + SCIM provisioning for limiting membership
- Retention 30 days ok for a pilot but needs sign-off from Privacy
- Need a vendor security questionnaire/attestation (SOC2/ISO links) and data residency info
Please open a security review ticket (link to SEC-234) and tag me.

jamal: We're not shipping server logs into sessions. Only client-side replay and custom non-PII events. SSO + SCIM are available in the plan we bought. I'll open SEC-234 and attach vendor docs + our masking config.

audrey: Platform ask — can you list the exact pages/events we intend to capture for the pilot? We should also add a guardrail so any form field with `type=password` or `.sensitive` is excluded from capture. Example FullStory exclude snippet:
```javascript
// FullStory privacy config
window['_fs_debug'] = false;
window['_fs_ready'] = function() {
  FS.setUserVars({ email: '[REDACTED]' });
  FS.privacy("maskAllTextInputs");
  FS.privacy("excludeElement", document.querySelector('input[type=password]'));
};
```

security-bot: SECURITY NOTE: Please attach SEC-234 and the vendor questionnaire to this thread. Ensure that the inventory entry is updated (vendor-inventory@redwood). Automated reminder in 48h if no update.

kate: From security side — conditional approval for a limited prod pilot (2 weeks) with the following requirements met first:
1) SSO + RBAC enforced (only support@redwood group)
2) Redaction config merged and verified in staging
3) Vendor questionnaire + SOC2 link attached to SEC-234
4) Inventory entry created with retention = 30d
If all that is in place, you have my :+1: to proceed. After the pilot we'll reassess for longer retention or wider access.

jamal: Thanks — I'll open SEC-234, create a PR with the redaction snippet, add the inventory entry, and ping here when done. Will tag @kate and @audrey.

ops-bot: Vendor access ticket created: VEND-8910. Assigned to jamal. Status: awaiting security review.

maria: Awesome, thanks. I'll prepare a short runbook for support on what they can/cannot view and how to request expanded access after pilot. :memo:

jamal: Great — will follow up with PR + links in this thread. Appreciate the quick checks! :rocket:
